    "title": "K-th Lexicographical Happy String",
    "category": "Backtracking",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "A happy string consists only of the characters 'a', 'b', and 'c', with no two adjacent characters being equal. Given integers N and K, determine the K-th lexicographically smallest happy string of length N. If fewer than K happy strings exist, print an empty string.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integers N and K.",
    "output": "Print the required happy string.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 10 \u2022 1 \u2264 K \u2264 3 \u00d7 2^(N\u22121)"
